Feature: Channel-wise Biosimilar Sales Performance Analysis

  This feature analyzes the sales performance of biosimilar brands (kanjinti, mvasi, riabni) across different channels (online, retail, mobile) using the purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack table. The analysis includes only sales data within 36 months from a specified cdl_effective_date, aggregates sales metrics, and presents results grouped by key attributes.

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the Source Table is "purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack"
    And the brands to analyze are "kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"
    And the channels to analyze are "online", "retail", "mobile"
    And the key attributes for grouping are "brand_normalized_name", "normalized_name", "market_normalized_name", "competitor_flag", "channel_name"
    And the sales metrics to aggregate are "integrated_units", "integrated_normalized_units", "integrated_dollars"
    And the time window is 36 months from the provided "cdl_effective_date"
    And the "cdl_effective_date" is in string format "yyyy-MM-dd"
    And only records with valid, non-null "cdl_effective_date" are included

  Scenario Outline: Happy Path - Aggregate sales metrics for valid biosimilar brands within 36 months
    Given the table contains records with brand_normalized_name "<brand>"
    And the channel_name is "<channel>"
    And the cdl_effective_date is a valid string in "yyyy-MM-dd" format
    And the transaction_timestamp is within 36 months from cdl_effective_date
    When the data is filtered for brand_normalized_name in ["kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"]
    And the data is filtered for channel_name in ["online", "retail", "mobile"]
    And the data is filtered for transaction_timestamp between cdl_effective_date and cdl_effective_date + 36 months
    And the data is grouped by brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name
    And the sales metrics are aggregated by sum of integrated_units, sum of integrated_normalized_units, sum of integrated_dollars
    Then the output contains a row for each unique combination of brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name
    And the output values for integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, integrated_dollars are the correct sums for the group

    Examples:
      | brand     | channel | cdl_effective_date |
      | kanjinti  | online  | 2021-01-01         |
      | mvasi     | retail  | 2022-03-15         |
      | riabni    | mobile  | 2020-07-30         |

  Scenario Outline: Error Path - Invalid or Null cdl_effective_date
    Given the table contains records with brand_normalized_name "<brand>"
    And the channel_name is "<channel>"
    And the cdl_effective_date is "<cdl_effective_date>"
    When the cdl_effective_date is null or not in "yyyy-MM-dd" format
    Then the record is excluded from the analysis
    And an error is logged in purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_invalid_cdl_effective_date_log with error_message "Invalid cdl_effective_date format"

    Examples:
      | brand     | channel | cdl_effective_date |
      | kanjinti  | online  | null              |
      | mvasi     | retail  | 2022/03/15        |
      | riabni    | mobile  | 15-07-2020        |

  Scenario Outline: Error Path - Transaction Timestamp Outside 36-Month Window
    Given the table contains records with brand_normalized_name "<brand>"
    And the channel_name is "<channel>"
    And the cdl_effective_date is "<cdl_effective_date>"
    And the transaction_timestamp is "<transaction_timestamp>"
    When the transaction_timestamp is not between cdl_effective_date and cdl_effective_date + 36 months
    Then the record is excluded from the analysis

    Examples:
      | brand     | channel | cdl_effective_date | transaction_timestamp |
      | kanjinti  | online  | 2021-01-01         | 2024-02-02           |
      | mvasi     | retail  | 2022-03-15         | 2025-04-01           |
      | riabni    | mobile  | 2020-07-30         | 2023-08-01           |

  Scenario Outline: Error Path - Brand Not in Target List
    Given the table contains records with brand_normalized_name "<brand>"
    And the channel_name is "<channel>"
    And the cdl_effective_date is "<cdl_effective_date>"
    When the brand_normalized_name is not in ["kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"]
    Then the record is excluded from the analysis

    Examples:
      | brand      | channel | cdl_effective_date |
      | herceptin  | online  | 2021-01-01         |
      | avastin    | retail  | 2022-03-15         |
      | rituxan    | mobile  | 2020-07-30         |

  Scenario Outline: Error Path - Channel Not in Target List
    Given the table contains records with brand_normalized_name "<brand>"
    And the channel_name is "<channel>"
    And the cdl_effective_date is "<cdl_effective_date>"
    When the channel_name is not in ["online", "retail", "mobile"]
    Then the record is excluded from the analysis

    Examples:
      | brand     | channel   | cdl_effective_date |
      | kanjinti  | hospital  | 2021-01-01         |
      | mvasi     | specialty | 2022-03-15         |
      | riabni    | mail      | 2020-07-30         |

  Scenario: Output Format Validation
    Given the analysis is complete
    When the output is generated
    Then the output is a table with columns: brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, sum_integrated_units, sum_integrated_normalized_units, sum_integrated_dollars
    And each row represents a unique combination of the grouping attributes
    And all aggregated values are integers (for units) and decimals (for dollars)
    And the output is suitable for export as CSV or table view

  Scenario: Data Validation Rules
    Given the table contains records for analysis
    When the data is processed
    Then cdl_effective_date must be a non-null string in "yyyy-MM-dd" format
    And transaction_timestamp must be a valid timestamp
    And integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, integrated_dollars must be non-negative integers or decimals
    And competitor_flag must be boolean (true/false)
    And channel_name must be one of ["online", "retail", "mobile"]
    And brand_normalized_name must be one of ["kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"]

  Scenario: Logging Invalid Records
    Given a record is excluded due to invalid cdl_effective_date
    When the record is processed
    Then the record is written to purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_invalid_cdl_effective_date_log
    And the error_message column contains a description of the error

  Scenario: No Data for Brand/Channel
    Given the table contains no records for brand_normalized_name "<brand>" and channel_name "<channel>" within the 36-month window
    When the analysis is performed
    Then the output does not contain a row for that brand/channel combination

    Examples:
      | brand     | channel |
      | kanjinti  | online  |
      | mvasi     | retail  |
      | riabni    | mobile  |
